  "Number": 15,
  "Question": "If \\(3^p + 3^4 = 90\\), \\(2^r + 44 = 76\\), and \\(5^3 + 6^s = 1421\\), what is the product of \\(p\\), \\(r\\), and \\(s\\)?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(27\\)",
    "B": "\\(40\\)",
    "C": "\\(50\\)",
    "D": "\\(70\\)",
    "E": "\\(90\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Subtract the known addend in each equation to leave a single power. Since \\(3^4=81\\) and \\(5^3=125\\), we obtain\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n3^p&=90-81=9=3^2,\\\\\n2^r&=76-44=32=2^5,\\\\\n6^s&=1421-125=1296=6^4.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nFor the last equality, \\(6\\cdot6\\cdot6\\cdot6=36\\cdot36=1296\\).\n\nThus \\(p=2\\), \\(r=5\\), and \\(s=4\\). Their product is\n\\[\np\\cdot r\\cdot s=2\\cdot5\\cdot4=40,\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
